block and Uint32 indices; real normals must be recomputed from triangle winding.\ntype: project\ncategory: common_pitfall\nkeywords:\n  - \"Human Atlas binary format\"\n  - \"atlas normals corrupt\"\n  - \"Uint32 index buffer\"\n  - \"bodyParts3D mesh decoding\"\nusage_scenarios:\n  - \"Decoding portal/anatomy BodyParts3D geometry\"\n  - \"Building or debugging the movement rig meshes\"\n---\n\nThe per-part `normals` block referenced by `portal/anatomy/models/atlas.json` is not a usable normal field: each component occupies only 2 bytes, and reading it as float32 yields values like `-8.17e34`. Only the sign is meaningful.\n\n**Why:** the atlas was optimised for display, where the renderer derives normals itself; the packed block is a leftover.\n\n**How to apply:** when decoding a part, read `positions` as float32 (3 per vertex) and `indices` as **Uint32** from `part.indices`, then accumulate area-weighted face normals from the triangle winding and normalise. Do not trust the `normals` offset for anything beyond vertex count.\n","file_path":"/home/runner/.qwen/projects/-home-runner-work-zero-one-workbench-zero-one-workbench/memory/project/atlas-normals-unusable.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":42202,"output_tokens":372,"cache_read_input_tokens":41472,"total_tokens":42574}}},{"type":"user","uuid":"181f586e-cf87-4d04-85d1-0938e1897699","session_id":"cef6745e-92bb-4fe4-9624-333962f2ed08","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_LAwQDYQzNOM9oWn6PRqe1194","is_error":true,"content":"File /home/runner/.qwen/projects/-home-runner-work-zero-one-workbench-zero-one-workbench/memory/project/atlas-normals-unusable.md has not been read in this session. Use the read_file tool first to load the current content (read the full file — overwriting replaces every byte, so any unseen bytes would be discarded) before overwriting it."}]}},{"type":"assistant","uuid":"a92b3529-1b1a-41b5-91fa-6460d4de4da9"